-- title:
--   Étale truncations of a flat unramified local algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a Noetherian commutative local ring and let $D$ be a commutative local ring equipped with a $V$-algebra structure whose structure map $V \to D$ is a local homomorphism and makes $D$ flat as a $V$-module. Assume that the ideal of $D$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_V$ is exactly $\mathfrak m_D$, and that the induced residue field extension $\kappa(D)/\kappa(V)$ is finite as a module and separable as an algebra. Let $m$ be a natural number with $m > 0$. Then the algebra $(V/\mathfrak m_V^{\,m}) \otimes_V D$ over $V/\mathfrak m_V^{\,m}$, with its canonical base-change algebra structure, is étale in the sense of Mathlib's `Algebra.Etale`, that is, formally étale and of finite presentation. (Through the isomorphism $(V/\mathfrak m_V^{\,m}) \otimes_V D \cong D/\mathfrak m_V^{\,m}D$ this is the assertion that each truncation $D_m$ is étale over $V_m = V/\mathfrak m_V^{\,m}$.)
--
--   This is the standard statement that a flat local algebra which is unramified in the sense $\mathfrak m_V D = \mathfrak m_D$, with finite separable residue extension, becomes finite étale after truncating the base at a power of its maximal ideal. It feeds the local deformation-theoretic lifting step [`IsLocalRing.existsUnique_algHom_residue_eq_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isNilpotent_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.existsUnique_algHom_residue_eq_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isNilpotent_maximalIdeal), where unique lifting of algebra maps along nilpotent thickenings is deduced from formal étaleness.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_Etale_quotient_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isSeparable.lean

